        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Details on isotopic vectors for biogeochemical variables:"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                142,
                131,
                539,
                146
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Methanogenesis pathway: To characterize the "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C H } _ { 4 } , \\ \\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C O } _ { 2 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": ", and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { \\alpha } _ { \\mathrm { { { d } \\alpha } } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "values of acetoclastic and hydrogenotrophic methanogenesis we used the center points of the fields for these two pathways in Figure 8 of Whiticar (1999). Specifically, for acetoclastic methanogenesis we used the following values: "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { \\delta } = - 6 0 \\% \\mathbf { \\delta } 0 \\mathbf { \\delta } \\mathrm { ; ~ } \\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathbf { C } \\mathbf { - } \\mathbf { C O } _ { 2 } = - 1 8 \\% \\mathbf { \\delta } 0 \\mathbf { \\delta } \\mathrm { ; ~ }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { \\vec { a } } _ { \\mathrm { C } } = 1 . 0 4 4"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": ". For hydrogenotrophic methanogenesis we used the following values: "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C H } _ { 4 } = - 7 5 \\% \\mathrm { o } ; \\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C O } _ { 2 } = 0 \\% \\mathrm { o } ;"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { \\alpha } _ { \\mathbf { C } } = 1 . 0 8 1"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": ". These values are approximate, as discussed in the text in section 3.4, but are frequently applied as end-member values for acetoclastic and hydrogenotrophic methanogenesis in environmental studies."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                140,
                160,
                856,
                266
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "To characterize the "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H } _ { 4 , \\mathrm { W 0 } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "value for acetoclastic and hydrogenotrophic methanogenesis we used the intercept of the freshwater "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "and marine "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "fields of Figure 10 of Whiticar (1999) with a "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H } \\cdot"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "_ \\mathrm { H _ { 2 } O }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "value of "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "0 \\text{‰}"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Specifically, for acetoclastic methanogenesis we used a value of -330‰, and for hydrogenotrophic methanogenesis we used a value of "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "- 2 3 0 \\text{‰}"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": ". These values are approximate, and as discussed in section 3.4 the role of methanogenesis pathway in controlling "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "has been questioned (Waldron et al., 1998;Waldron et al., 1999). However, these values represent the expected values under the paradigm that methanogenesis pathway does in fact control "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": ". As discussed in Sections 3.3 and 3.4, in reality differences in "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H } _ { 4 , \\mathrm { W 0 } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "between pathways likely vary as a function of the "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\ S ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "of acetate, as well as differences in the kinetic isotope effect and enzymatic reversibility associated with these pathways."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                140,
                266,
                856,
                404
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "C H _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Oxidation: To characterize the "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C H } _ { 4 } , \\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C O } _ { 2 } ."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { \\alpha } _  \\mathrm { { { d } \\mathrm { { c } \\} } } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "values of oxidized "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "we used the center points of the field for methane oxidation in Figure 8 of Whiticar (1999). Specifically, we used the following values: "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C H } _ { 4 } = - 4 0 \\% ; \\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C O } _ { 2 } = - 2 5 \\% \\mathrm { o } ;"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { a } _ { \\mathrm { C } } = 1 . 0 1 6"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "These values are approximate, as discussed in the text in section 3.4, but are frequently applied as end-member values for oxidized "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "in environmental studies. To characterize the "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H } _ { 4 , \\mathrm { W 0 } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "value for oxidized methane we used the prediction shown in Figure 5 of Whiticar (1999), specifically using a value of -150‰. This value, and the "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\bar { 8 } ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "value above, is consistent with model predictions of nearly complete, closed-system aerobic methane oxidation from Wang et al. (2016). The vectors shown in Figure 6 do not extend to this fully oxidized methane value in order to fit within the figure axes. Anaerobic "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "oxidation may have a different isotopic vector, but we did not consider this since aerobic CH4 oxidation is typically considered to be more prevalent in freshwater environments."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                140,
                415,
                856,
                580
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Gas-phase diffusion: We estimated the effects of gas phase diffusion using the equations presented by Chanton (2005). We specifically calculated diffusive fractionation for "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C O } _ { 2 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "in air. Gas-liquid diffusion isotopic fractionation is predicted to be much smaller by (Chanton, 2005), and we did not specifically calculate this. Diffusive fractionation for "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C O } _ { 2 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "in air is most likely to be important for environments with plant-mediated gas transport. We calculated the isotopic composition of residual gas left following diffusive gas loss, and we did not calculate the effects of progressive Rayleigh fractionation. The vector for diffused gas would extend in the opposite direction. Specific values for residual gas affected by diffusive gas, starting with the values for acetoclastic methanogenesis reported above, transport are as follows: "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C } \\mathrm { - } \\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 } = - 4 1 . 7 \\% \\mathrm { o } \\mathrm { o } ; \\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H } \\mathrm { - } \\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 , \\mathrm { W } 0 } = - 3 1 7 \\% \\mathrm { o } ; \\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C } \\mathrm { - } \\mathrm { C O } _ { 2 } = - 1 3 . 7 \\% \\mathrm { o } ;"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { a } _ { \\mathrm { C } } { = } 1 . 0 3 2"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                140,
                593,
                856,
                727
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Enzymatic reversibility: The effect of enzymatic reversibility or thermodynamic favorability on "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "isotopic fractionation is an intriguing idea that is not yet well constrained. These hypothesized effects are based on experiments wherein "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\bar { \\delta } ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - } \\mathrm { \\bar { C } H } _ { 4 } , \\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - } \\mathrm { C O } _ { 2 } ."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": ", and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { \\alpha } _ { \\mathrm { { { d } \\alpha } } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "values co-varied with estimates of Gibbs free energy (ΔG) (Valentine et al., 2004;Penning et al., 2005) or wherein "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "co-varied with methane production rate (Valentine et al., 2004). These effects, at least for "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H } _ { 4 } ,"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "are also supported by isotopic modeling (Stolper et al., 2015), and co-variation of "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { \\alpha } _ { \\mathrm { Q H } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "with clumped isotope measurements of "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H _ { 4 } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "(Stolper et al., 2015; Douglas et al., 2017). Defining isotopic vectors for this variable is challenging because it has not been studied experimentally in terms of "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\ S ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H _ { 4 } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "simultaneously. We use the experimental results of (Penning et al., 2005), specifically focusing on an experiment with a cellulose substrate, to define the changes in "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\ S ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C H _ { 4 } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "(decrease of 27‰), "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\ S ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - C O } _ { 2 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "(increase of 8‰), and "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { \\alpha } _ { \\mathrm { { { d } \\mathrm { { C } } } } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "(increase of 0.04) values as the methanogenesis reaction ΔG shifts from being more favorable (-80 kJ/mol)"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                140,
                739,
                857,
                909
            ]
