    [
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "to less favourable (-20 kJ/mol). These results are similar to changes in "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { \\alpha } _ { \\mathrm { { { d } \\mathrm { { C } } } } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "as a function of "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { H } _ { 2 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "partial pressure, and therefore ΔG, observed by (Valentine et al., 2004), although in that study differences in "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C } ."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C O } _ { 2 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "were minimal. We define changes in "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\ S ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H _ { 4 } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "based on observed changes as a function of "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathrm { C H } _ { 4 }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "production rate by (Valentine et al., 2004), specifically an increase of approximately 94‰ at low production rates (~250 µmol/hour) relative to high production rates (~700 µmol/hour). Since the carbon and hydrogen isotope effects were not observed in the same experiment, their correspondence is speculative, and requires further validation. We include this effect in Figure "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "^ { 6 , }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "despite its uncertainty, for the sake of discussing a comprehensive set of possible variables influencing "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\delta ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { H - C H _ { 4 } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                140,
                92,
                856,
                212
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "It is important to note that the enzymatic reversibility effect has only been studied in terms of hydrogenotrophic methanogenesis, both experimentally (Valentine et al., 2004;Penning et al., 2005) and in models (Stolper et al., 2015). It is unclear whether it also applies, and whether it would have the same magnitude, in acetoclastic methanogenesis, "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "_ { \\mathrm { o r } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "in environmental systems with multiple pathways of methanogenesis. As shown in Figure "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "^ { 6 , }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "the direction and magnitude of the proposed isotopic vectors for the enzymatic reversibility effect is similar to that inferred for changes in the pathway of methanogenesis, and given the uncertainty described above, at present these two variables cannot be differentiated on the basis of isotopic measurements in environmental systems."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                140,
                210,
                857,
                328
            ]
        },
